{"game_id":2026020290,"away":"DET","home":"STL","split":{"name":"Dvorský","side":1,"sec":1572},"lede":"St. Louis had last change, so Jim Montgomery picked most of these matchups. St. Louis played without Adam Jiříček and Aleksanteri Kaskimäki and lost Dalibor Dvorský after 6:12 of the second. Detroit played without Carter Mazur and John Leonard.","notes":[{"kind":"match","head":"Thomas’s line drew DeBrincat’s line","text":"Jim Montgomery sent Holloway, Thomas and Snuggerud out for 8:11 of their 15:36 at 5-on-5 against DeBrincat, Finnie and Arvidsson (52%, about 30% with no line matching), and they had the better of the chances, 0.49 to 0.04 expected goals. St. Louis scored one of its three goals then."},{"kind":"swing","head":"One matchup paid off","text":"Holloway, Thomas and Snuggerud kept drawing Detroit’s second line, Brandsegg-Nygård, Copp and Raymond. In those 3:34 St. Louis had 0.80 expected goals to Detroit’s 0.04."},{"kind":"exit","head":"After Dvorský left, the lines changed","text":"McTavish went from 22% to 35% and Neighbours from 24% to 32% of St. Louis’s 5-on-5 time, and Johnston dropped from 23% to 14%."},{"kind":"result","head":"And it went worse","text":"St. Louis had 1.28 to 0.34 expected goals at 5-on-5 before Dvorský left and 1.88 to 1.01 after. St. Louis led for most of that stretch, though, and a team ahead usually sits back, so the score explains part of it."}],"foot":"Jim Montgomery matched about as hard as in his other home games: each line spent 44% of its time against one opposing line, against 36% to 71% in his first seven.","periods":{"all":{"0":{"rows":[{"label":"L1","names":["DeBrincat","Finnie","Arvidsson"],"sec":935,"mixed":5,"vs":[491,82,257,105],"xgf":0.45,"xga":0.58,"gf":0,"ga":1,"cells":[[0.04,0.49,0,1],[0.03,0.0,0,0],[0.38,0.09,0,0],[0.01,0.0,0,0]]},{"label":"L2","names":["Brandsegg-Nygård","Copp","Raymond"],"sec":924,"mixed":5,"vs":[214,225,218,267],"xgf":0.65,"xga":1.14,"gf":1,"ga":0,"cells":[[0.04,0.8,0,0],[0.22,0.15,1,0],[0.